 "phase": "L5 (loading time): bitmap effects without whole-table copies",
 "change": "OriginalApplicationBitmapInputs.response and OriginalApplicationGraphics.bitmap ran their work on a rollback copy (var next = self); every case checks before it stores, so a throw happens only before the first change, and they now run in place. The catalog session's effect and bitmap-construction paths copied the graphics owner and the bitmap inputs out of their state and stored them back; they now take each out of the state (nil while it changes, restored in a defer), so the owner is the only reference and its dictionaries change in place. Each bitmap effect copied the growing image, surface and DC tables and the graphics' resource tables before.",
 "profile": "A12 ml-l4b-loadprof: _NativeDictionary.copy 10.4% inclusive (Graphics.create setValue 4.8%, performBitmap modify 2.3%, BitmapInputs.perform setValue 2.2%, Attempt.sound 0.8%)",
 "review": "independent read-only reviewer: no correctness problem; every throw in BitmapInputs.perform and Graphics.performBitmap/create precedes the first change to self (stretch changes a local copy stored last); consume leaves the owner unchanged on every throw (window and front keep their rollback copies); nothing reads the state's optional while it is nil; no exclusivity overlap; all 42 rejections of the new test fail for the stated reason",
 "notes": "The measured gain (12.3 s on the A12) is larger than the profile share (~4.5 s): the copies also cost allocation, page faults and cache misses that the profile charged to other frames.",
